{{Quote|The droid was sent to Vassek based on intel from a captured smuggler. It scanned a settlement on the planet for six weeks, recording conversations between local farmers.|Viper 058-V-2353's report|<ref name="Outlaws" />}}
A '''settlement''' was established on<ref name="Outlaws" /> the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]<ref name="BMF 65">{{BuildFalconCite|65|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> [[planet]] [[Vassek]] by the [[time]] of the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Outlaws" /> At some point by [[3 ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> the [[viper probe droid]] [[Viper 058-V-2353]] [[Investigation on Vassek|spent]] six [[Standard week|weeks]] recording conversations between local [[farmer]]s at the [[City|settlement]], having been sent to the world after receiving intel from a [[Unidentified smuggler (Roni)|smuggler]] the [[Galactic Empire]] had captured. The [[probe droid]] learned via their observations that the farmer [[Roni]] was planning to [[Thief|steal]] Imperial generators, which ultimately resulted in the arrest of the latter and two of their [[Roni's family|family]] members by an [[Unidentified Imperial Security Bureau agent (Vassek)|Imperial Security Bureau agent]]. Afterward, Viper 058-V-2353 departed the settlement for the Imperial [[space station]] [[Derosha Six]], where a report of the [[droid]]'s time on Vassek was then kept on a [[datapad]].<ref name="Outlaws" />

{{GameMechanics|Star Wars Outlaws}}
In 3 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate" /> the outlaw [[Kay Vess]] [[Infiltration of Derosha Six|infiltrated]] Derosha Six and read the datapad mentioning the settlement while evading Imperial personnel.<ref name="Outlaws" />
{{EndGame}}

==Behind the scenes==
The settlment was mentioned via datapad in the [[2024]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]'', developed by [[Massive Entertainment]].<ref name="Outlaws" />

